# nr-office-comrs-recorder: the recorder package of crates/mixdog-office-com and its registry test.

Nothing here was compiled (no cargo run by this task). The new package is `native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/recorder`
(`mixdog-office-com-recorder`, a cdylib and rlib, Windows only: elsewhere its lib is empty). It uses no crate that is not
already in the lock and has its own FFI (no `windows` feature, no `windows-sys`).

## native/core/Cargo.toml

`[workspace] members`: after `"crates/mixdog-office-com",` add

    "crates/mixdog-office-com/recorder",

No `[workspace.dependencies]` entry: nothing depends on the recorder.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (owned by an earlier task; the explicit test list needs the new test)

After the `[[test]] name = "pswire"` block add

    [[test]]
    name = "registry_source"
    path = "tests/registry_source.rs"

No new dependency: the test uses `regex`, `serde_json`, `sha2` and `mixdog-testkit` (`read`, `read_string`, `exists`), which
the crate already lists.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Add the package (a `cargo update -w --offline` writes it):

    [[package]]
    name = "mixdog-office-com-recorder"
    version = "1.5.0"
    dependencies = [
     "mixdog-office-com",
     "mixdog-workspace-hack",
     "serde_json",
    ]

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

No external crate or feature is new (serde_json and mixdog-office-com are already unified). Run the hakari check after the
manifest edit and take its output if it asks for a line for the new member.

## Not wired

No protocol row, no `SERVICE_PENDING` name, no desktop change. `crates/mixdog-testkit/tests/cfg_test_guard.rs` lists only
`mixdog-core` and `mixdog-core-session`; the recorder's `cfg(test)` items are a thread-local capture and test fixtures that
nothing else uses, so no entry is needed.

## What the lead should compile and run

* `cargo build -p mixdog-office-com-recorder --offline` on Windows and `cargo clippy -p mixdog-office-com-recorder --all-targets -- -D warnings`
  (the crate's unit tests build fake `IDispatch` and `IEnumVARIANT` objects of the C ABI in process: they start no Office,
  no PowerShell and write no file).
* `cargo nextest run -p mixdog-office-com --test registry_source` (reads the embedded `assets/office-com-host.ps1` and,
  when it exists, `C:/Project/mixdog`; no Office needed).
* The recording itself (`recorder/record-office-com.mjs --area selftest`) needs Microsoft Office and is not part of any run.
